Package: bicountbrms
Title: Custom 'brms' Families for Paired Counts
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-11-15
Authors@R: c(
    person("Adam N. H.", "Smith", , "anhsmith@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0059-6206")),
    person("The Nature Conservancy", role = "fnd"),
    person("Belize Blue Bonds for Ocean Conservation", role = "fnd"),
    person("Belize Fund for a Sustainable Future", role = "fnd")
  )
Description: Provides custom 'brms' families for pairs of counts that two
    sources, such as methods, observers, or instruments, each record on the
    same unit. The pair is modelled by trivariate reduction with Poisson
    (bipois()) or negative-binomial (binegbin()) components: the count from
    each source is the sum of a latent count of events recorded by both
    sources and a latent count of events recorded by that source alone. The
    constructors bipois_partialobs() and binegbin_partialobs() also fit
    partially paired designs, in which source 2 records every unit and
    source 1 only a subset of units; the missing counts of source 1 can then
    be imputed conditional on the counts recorded by source 2.
    mfd_to_dpars() and dpars_to_mfd() convert the native parameters to and from
    the congruence–bias coordinates: the midpoint of the two expected counts,
    the congruence, and the source bias. bf_mfd() writes the 'brms' formula in
    the congruence–bias coordinates, and rbicount() simulates pairs of counts
    from the model.
